  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q58-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "58",
    "prompt": "Given $2\\alpha+\\beta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$,",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q58-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that\n\n$$\\tan\\beta=\\frac{1-2\\tan\\alpha-\\tan^2\\alpha}{1+2\\tan\\alpha-\\tan^2\\alpha}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\tan\\beta=\\dfrac{1-2\\tan\\alpha-\\tan^2\\alpha}{1+2\\tan\\alpha-\\tan^2\\alpha}$.\n\nExpand $\\tan(\\frac{\\pi}{4}-2\\alpha)$, then substitute the tangent double-angle formula.",
          "worked": "Since $\\beta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}-2\\alpha$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\beta&=\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}-2\\alpha\\right)\\\\\\tan\\beta&=\\frac{1-\\tan 2\\alpha}{1+\\tan 2\\alpha}\\\\\\tan\\beta&=\\frac{1-\\dfrac{2\\tan\\alpha}{1-\\tan^2\\alpha}}{1+\\dfrac{2\\tan\\alpha}{1-\\tan^2\\alpha}}\\\\\\tan\\beta&=\\frac{1-\\tan^2\\alpha-2\\tan\\alpha}{1-\\tan^2\\alpha+2\\tan\\alpha}\\\\\\tan\\beta&=\\frac{1-2\\tan\\alpha-\\tan^2\\alpha}{1+2\\tan\\alpha-\\tan^2\\alpha}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q58-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find the exact value of $\\tan\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt2-1$.\n\nSet $\\beta=0$ and $\\alpha=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$ in part a, then take the positive root of the resulting quadratic.",
          "worked": "Set $\\beta=0$ and $\\alpha=\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}$, and let $t=\\tan\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}$. Part a gives\n\n$$\\begin{align*}0&=\\frac{1-2t-t^2}{1+2t-t^2}\\\\1-2t-t^2&=0\\\\t^2+2t-1&=0\\\\t&=\\frac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{4+4}}{2}\\\\t&=-1\\pm\\sqrt2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}$ is in the first quadrant, $t>0$. Thus $\\tan\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}=\\sqrt2-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      }
    ]
  },
